From 359cc6549bfd8363485e7ad32d78b02e65cee83c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BHARATH CHANDRA VADDARAM <bharath.vbcr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:28:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Replay field-path effects across a closure boundary and
 test the edge shapes

The closure summary carries the path under each captured variable, so `h.w.Write` in a closure
meets `h.w.Close` in its creator and the reverse, on the same per-path slot the creator uses. A
closure that stores to a captured variable (or to a path in it) now contributes neither writes nor
closes for it: the close may be of the resource the store put there, and replaying it on the
creator's flag reported `w = open(); w.Close()` inside a closure after the creator had written w.

errc7ddedge pins each edge: a closure that writes then replaces the variable under a creator's
deferred Close is a MISS (one slot per variable, and a deferred close is judged against the slot at
exit, so replaying the write would also report the reassign-in-body shape that
advfvbreak3b3c pins as clean), its no-closure twin reports, field paths in both directions,
a different field, a by-reference holder, a replaced field, and a closing closure called twice,
deferred, and in a loop, each with exactly one report per line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
